# ── [TASK-00] large binaries never enter git ──────────────────────────────────
# Small artifacts stay trackable: results/**/*.json, results/**/*.csv,
# results/**/gates/phi_e*.npz, figures_data/
*.pth
*.pt
results/**/ckpt/
results/**/attn/
results/**/*_norms.npz
# [TASK-08] smoke-run outputs never become results
results/smoke/
# [TASK-09] per-rank prediction shards are transient eval scratch
results/**/eval_shards/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
wandb/
# [TASK-I2] B2: the EVALUATION sweep's raw per-image records stay on the HPC,
# beside results/**/*_norms.npz. 19 runs x 10 000 images x up to 11
# (condition, stage) pairs is ~90 MB of parquet that nothing downstream reads
# twice: the tables, maps.npz and figures_data/frozen/I2_evaluation_primary.npz
# are committed and every reported number regenerates from them. Each run's
# run_meta.json IS committed and records the sha256 and byte size of the files
# left behind, so a number still traces to an identified file.
# The CALIBRATION sweep is small and stays fully committed.
results/frozen/I2_terminal/evaluation/*/records.parquet
results/frozen/I2_terminal/evaluation/*/diag.parquet
results/frozen/I2_terminal/evaluation/*/records.csv
results/frozen/I2_terminal/evaluation/*/diag.csv
# [TASK-B/I3, I4] the SAME policy, named per work package rather than by a
# `results/frozen/**/records.parquet` wildcard, so that a small sweep on a
# small split stays committable by default and dropping a raw record file out
# of git is always a deliberate line in this file.
#
# It was NOT here when I3 Phase B landed, and 113 MiB of I3 parquet went to
# the remote on 2026-09-17 as a result (16 files; the blobs are in history and
# stay there). These lines exist so I4 — another ~130 MiB — does not repeat
# it. The committed run_meta.json records each file's sha256 and byte size,
# and figures_data/frozen/I3_primary.npz / I4_primary.npz carry the per-image
# values every reported number is resampled from.
results/frozen/I3_gate_edits/*/*/records.parquet
results/frozen/I3_gate_edits/*/*/diag.parquet
results/frozen/I3_gate_edits/*/*/records.csv
results/frozen/I3_gate_edits/*/*/diag.csv
results/frozen/I4_perturbation/*/*/records.parquet
results/frozen/I4_perturbation/*/*/diag.parquet
results/frozen/I4_perturbation/*/*/records.csv
results/frozen/I4_perturbation/*/*/diag.csv
# [TASK-A/I1] the per-token norm fields stay on the cluster: float32
# [10 000 x 196] per stage per run is ~8 MB, ~1 GB over 19 runs x 4 stages x
# two splits. Everything derived from them — the frequency maps, the packed
# per-image indicators, the counts and the thresholds — is in the SIBLING
# maps_<stage>.npz, which is committed (~270 kB per stage per run) and which
# this pattern deliberately does not match. Each run's run_meta.json records
# the sha256 and byte size of the norm dumps left behind.
results/frozen/**/norms_*.npz
